# CAP — Granular Capability Migration Rules
File: openOODA/oodac/docs/CAP_LEGACY_SUPERSEDE_REMOVAL_TODO.oot

Product check no longer accepts a broad `NetCap` / `FsCap` / `SysCap` /
`AllocCap` token as a supersede for the granular kind a sealed op needs.
Callers must declare the granular capability they actually use.

This file is the migration rule table. It is not a live caller inventory.
Product CLI, check, and emit-c sources live under `cli/`, `check/`, and
`emit/c/`. Residual ISA CLIs are not product.

## Migration rules

| Sealed op (granular required) | Broad cap | Replace with |
|---|---|---|
| `fetch` / `http_get` / `net_get` / `net_connect` / `tls_connect` | `&NetCap` | `&TcpCap` |
| `tcp_connect` / `tcp_write` / `tcp_read` / `tcp_close` | `&NetCap` | `&TcpCap` |
| `tcp_bind` | `&NetCap` | `&BindCap` |
| `bind_udp` / `udp_recv` / `udp_send` | `&NetCap` | `&UdpCap` |
| `read_file` / `fs_read` / `path_exists` / `file_size` | `&FsCap` | `&FsReadCap` |
| `write_file` / `fs_write` | `&FsCap` | `&FsWriteCap` |
| `sys_exec` / `process_exec` / `sys_spawn` / `sys_wait` / `sys_kill` | `&SysCap` | `&ProcessCap` |
| `arena_create` / `arena_alloc` / `arena_reset` | `&AllocCap` | `&ArenaCap` |

`&NetCap` is reserved for `sock_raw` / `raw_socket`.
`&SysCap` is reserved for residual OS ops (`sys_epoll_create`,
`sys_inotify_init`, `sys_prctl`, `oo_rlimit_set_*`, `landlock_restrict`).
`&AllocCap` is reserved for `alloc_bytes` / `free_bytes` / `malloc` /
`free`.

A function that both reads and writes the filesystem takes BOTH
`&FsReadCap` and `&FsWriteCap`. There is no broad `&FsCap` alias.

Product `cli/cli_build.oo`, `cli/cli_emit.oo`, and `cli/cli_parse.oo`
already take granular `&FsReadCap` / `&FsWriteCap` / `&ProcessCap` /
`&EnvCap`. Rebuild the compiler after any check-cap change:

```
$ bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build oodac/main.oo oodac_bin.core
```
